# L5R 5E — CHILDREN OF THE FIVE WINDS (LORE): PASSAGES

**Version:** 0.5.1
**Source:** Children of the Five Winds (Legend of the Five Rings Roleplaying Game, 5th Edition)
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games

---

> **Adventure Seeds**
>
> Throughout this book, you will find sidebars like this one presenting adventure seeds for GMs. If you are a player, you might want to avoid reading these, as doing so could spoil things should your GM adopt any of the ideas! If you are a GM, you can expand on these seeds to create full-fledged adventures, take bits and pieces, or simply use them for inspiration.
>
> Hook The hook provides the context for starting the adventure and introduces the important NPCs. We also provide a suggested way to involve the PCs in events, which you can tailor to fit your campaign.
>
> Rising Action In the next part of an adventure seed, we briefly describe the most likely way for events to escalate, further embroiling the PCs and raising the stakes.
>
> Climax Finally, we offer a likely climax for the adventure, whether it is a decisive encounter with an NPC or a difficult choice the PCs must make. By this point, the events of the adventure are likely to have taken unexpected turns based on the PCs’ actions, and you should feel free to modify the climax or resolve matters in whatever way fits the ongoing campaign.

