#### The Utaku Family Mon

#### A simple, plain circle, symbolizing the stillness and silence of the family founder.

#### The Lands of the Utaku

##### Battle Maiden Castle

Yet more impressive than the castle’s blend of foreign and ancient architecture, its bell-shaped domes, or its constructed cascades is its greatest treasure: the Utaku ancestral stables. Often mistaken for a second keep, these stables house the breeding and training grounds of many different steeds. As the estate’s most important feature, the stables enjoy dedicated protective walls and remain under watchful guard at all times.

##### Utaku Seidō: The Shrine of Shimmering Grasses

#### Utaku Asagao

Gear (equipped): Shrine keeper robes (Physical 1, Supernatural 3, Ceremonial), offerings

Companion: Taiyo (see Utaku warhorse on page 143)

#### The Iuchi Family Mon

#### An open scroll, representing the Tao of Shinsei, which is used as the principle source that guides the Iuchi's celestial interpretations.

#### Culture and Traditions

Many Iuchi find a calling to serve their clan. Among these are the Disciples of the Horse Lord. Employing methods derived from the research of Iuchi Meiko, one of Iuchi’s children who accompanied the Purple Horde of Utaku Shiko, the Horse Lords are specialized Meishōdō Masters. Using horse-shaped meishōdō talismans, they can invoke the Fortune of Horses. By adorning horses with these trinkets, they have the ability to empower a samurai’s steed, to speak with horses directly, or even to summon an ethereal mount. The Iuchi Horse Lord Disciples are also foremost experts in equine medicine, and they have saved the lives of many injured steeds.

