### Rules for Otherworldly Encounters

#### Complicating Factors

- A rival spirit that hopes to form its own pact with the local mortals, allowing it to displace its enemy.
- A group of mortals who falsely believe the spirit to be a monster that needs to be removed and are spoiling for a fight.
- A conniving village head or lord who wants to exploit the situation to their own benefit by getting something petty or personal from the spirit (which might dissuade it from helping others or enrage it to lash out).
- A naïve individual who believes the spirit can solve a problem that is beyond its abilities and tries to monopolize its attention.
- A Tainted spirit (kansen) that has taken up residence in the region and is attempting to destabilize the situation to spread its influence during the chaos.
- A fraudulent exorcist who is trying to con one or more parties for the exorcist’s benefit.

#### New Actions

##### Compel

Description: You attempt to overpower a spirit by using its true name.

Activation: As a Scheme action targeting one spirit whose true name you know, you may make a TN 1 Theology (Void) check. You must be trained in the Way of Names to use this action.

Effects: If you succeed, you add 1 momentum point toward your current social objective. Then, the spirit must resist with a TN 3 Meditation check (Void 1). If it fails, you add a number of additional momentum points toward your current objective equal to its shortfall. If it succeeds, increase the TN of the next check it makes to resist the Compel action by 1 until the end of the scene. This effect is cumulative, increasing the TN by 1 each time.

##### Entice

Description: You attempt to win a spirit’s favor with a small offering.

Activation: As a Scheme action targeting one spirit, you may offer up an item of value and make a Theology check. The TN of this check is equal to the spirit’s intrigue conflict ranks minus the rarity of the item.

Effects: If you succeed, the spirit accepts the item, and you add 1 momentum point to an appropriate objective, plus 1 momentum point for every two bonus successes.

##### New Opportunities

Air (op) (op) (op): You ascertain a key detail about the spirit, such as the span of its domain, its current social objective, or the terms it requests in its pacts. If you are trained in the Way of Names, you can learn its true name instead.

Earth (op)+: Reduce the spirit’s momentum points toward its current social objective by 1. Additionally, you may reduce the spirit’s momentum points toward that objective by 1 per (op) (op) spent this way beyond the first.

Fire (op) (op): Treat your focus as 1 higher until the end of the scene.

Water (op) (op): Reduce the TN of your next check targeting the spirit by 1.

Void (op): Gain the Centered condition (see page 133).

### New Titles

#### Animal Handler

Assigned By: The GM, after a character has taken sufficient narrative steps to tame and train a suitable animal. At the bare minimum, this should involve making a successful Survival check as a downtime activity with a TN equal to the animal’s combat conflict ranks. One method of obtaining an animal companion is through the Animal Bond passion found in the core rulebook.

Instinctive Command (Title Ability): After you perform an action, you may receive 2 fatigue to have any number of your animal companions each take an action that shares a type with your action (your animal's actions are still limited to taking one action of each type per round).

