|---|---|
| The ifrit is an Otherworldly being. Once per scene as an action of the appropriate types, the ifrit may perform any one Fire invocation (other than Rise, Fire). It counts as succeeding with 3 bonus successes and 2 (op).<br>MANTLE OF SMOKE AND ASH Other characters treat the area at range 0–1 of the ifrit as Dangerous and Obscuring terrain.<br>SEARING CARESS When performing an Attack action check, the ifrit may spend (op) as follows: | Once per scene when making a check, Miya Tetsua may count his ranks in the skill used as being equal to his status rank. [They/Them] A shrine keeper of the Dragonfly Minor Clan, Tonbo Kuma is a member of the Tonbo family, which maintains the extensive shrine gardens in the City of the Rich Frog. The Dragonfly’s de facto leader within this city, Tonbo is a good friend of its governor, Miya Tetsua. |
| (op)+: The target and up to one other character per |  |

#### Daidoji Shin

(op) (op): Shin learns one of the target’s advantages or disadvantages of the target’s choice.

When making a Social skill (Fire) check, Shin may spend (op) in the following way:

Fire (op): One target gains the Dazed condition.

